om                              \r\n                                   deleted pods)                                                                                            \r\n                                 config:                                                                                                    \r\n                                   url: http://host.docker.internal:9954/loki/sse                                                           \r\n                                   mode: sse                                                                                                \r\n                               sregym-jaeger:                                                                                               \r\n                                 description: Distributed traces from Jaeger (service call graph, latency, errors)                          \r\n                                 config:                                                                                                    \r\n                                   url: http://host.docker.internal:9954/jaeger/sse                                                         \r\n                                   mode: sse                                                                                                \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n"]
[1292.852625, "o", "[10/23/26 10:35:51] INFO     all.holmesgpt.driver - HolmesGPT answer:                                                                       \r\n                             **ROOT CAUSE**                                                                                                 \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             - **Faulty component:** `Pod grafana-7b9cbf56f5-qd4qp` (part of the `grafana` Deployment) in namespace         \r\n                             **astronomy‑shop**                                                                                             \r\n                             - **Why it fails:** The Grafana container attempts to bind to `0.0.0.0:8080`. Port 8080 is already in use by   \r\n                             multiple other services in the demo (e.g., `checkout`, `cart`, `currency`, etc.). The bind error (`[Errno 98]  \r\n                             address in use`) forces Grafana to repeatedly restart, producing connection‑refused errors when it later tries \r\n                             to call its own HTTP API (`localhost:3000`). This is why the pod shows **3 restarts** and why the logs contain \r\n                             repeated `ERROR` and `WARNING` entries about the address conflict and failed HTTP calls.                       \r\n                             - **Evidence:**                                                                                                \r\n                               - Grafana pod status: `restartCount: 3`, `ready: true` (still running but repeatedly restarted).             \r\n                               - Logs (last hour, error‑filtered) contain:                                                                  \r\n                                 ```                                                                                                        \r\n                                 [Errno 98] error while attempting to bind on address ('0.0.0.0', 8080): address in use                     \r\n                                 Retry... connection refused to http://localhost:3000/api/admin/provisioning/...                            \r\n                                 ```                                                                                                        \r\n                               - Other services (checkout, cart, etc.) all expose `containerPort: 8080`, confirming the port conflict.      \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **FIX**                                                                                                        \r\n                             Change Grafana’s HTTP port to a free value (e.g., the default `3000`) by updating its Deployment/ConfigMap (or \r\n                             Helm values) to set `GF_SERVER_HTTP_PORT=3000` (or remove any custom port setting). Then redeploy Grafana. This\r\n                             eliminates the bind error, stops the restart loop, and restores the Grafana UI for the OpenTelemetry demo.     \r\n"]
